<h2>Delete local web data</h2>
<p>Delete individual notes, highlights, favorites, and reflections using the controls provided in Daily Breath. To remove all browser-only Daily Breath data, clear site data for <strong>beyondimagination.co.technology</strong> in your browser settings and uninstall the Daily Breath web app if installed. Clearing site data can also sign you out and remove other locally stored Beyond preferences for that browser.</p>

<h2>Delete local Apple app data</h2>
<p>Delete individual journal entries and scripture notes in the app. To remove all local app data, delete Daily Breath from the device. If Encrypted iCloud Sync was enabled, also disable sync in Daily Breath and use your Apple iCloud storage controls as needed. Deleting the app does not automatically delete a Beyond ID or transaction records maintained by an app store.</p>

<h2>Delete local Android app data</h2>
<p>Use the available journal controls for individual entries. To remove all on-device data, open Android Settings, choose Apps, select Daily Breath, then choose Storage &amp; cache and Clear storage; uninstalling the app also removes its private local data. Android backup is disabled for Daily Breath.</p>

<h2>Request deletion of account-linked Daily Breath data</h2>
<p>Email <a href="mailto:support@beyond-os.com?subject=Delete%20my%20Daily%20Breath%20data">support@beyond-os.com</a> from the email address connected to your Beyond ID with the subject <strong>Delete my Daily Breath data</strong>. State whether you want only Daily Breath records deleted or your entire Beyond ID account reviewed for deletion. We will verify the request before deleting eligible data and will explain any records that must be retained for purchase restoration, security, fraud prevention, accounting, disputes, or legal obligations.</p>

<h2>What an account-data request can cover</h2>
<p>A verified request may cover Daily Breath journal records stored on our servers, breathing and challenge activity, Academy progress, newsletter details, connected-app records, and other account-linked Daily Breath data. Local device or browser data must be removed on that device. Apple, Google, Amazon, Stripe, and iCloud records are controlled by those providers and may require a separate request to them.</p>

<h2>Other privacy requests</h2>
<p>You may use the same address to request access, correction, or export of eligible Daily Breath personal information. Include only the information needed to identify your account; never email a password, payment-card number, or authentication code.</p>

<p class="legal-note"><strong>Response process:</strong> We may ask you to confirm control of the connected email address or sign in before completing a request. Requests are handled within the period required by applicable law.</p>
